---
layout: default
pagination:
  data: library.entries
  size: 1
  alias: entry
permalink: "/library/{{ entry.id }}/"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ entry.name }} · {{ entry.category }} · Skills Library"
---
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/library/library.css">
<main class="library library-detail container" id="main-content">
<a class="library-back" href="/library/">← All skills & agents</a>
<header><p class="library-eyebrow">{{ entry.category }} / {{ entry.runtime }} / {{ entry.kind }}</p><h1>{{ entry.name }}</h1><p class="library-detail-description">{{ entry.description | skillInline | safe }}</p></header>
<section class="library-detail-setup"><h2>{{ 'Install this skill' if entry.kind == 'skill' else 'Set up this agent' }}</h2>
{% if entry.install %}<div class="library-command"><pre><code>{{ entry.install | escape }}</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy>Copy</button></div><p>Run inside your target project after this library is published. <a href="/library/#install">Installation guide and local preview →</a></p>
{% else %}<p>Download the packaged definition below and save it to <code>.claude/agents/{{ entry.name }}.md</code> in your target project. Review any existing file before replacing it. Companion skills are optional; the agent includes a direct-execution fallback. The Skills CLI does not install agent definitions.</p>{% endif %}
<p class="library-file-links"><a class="library-button" href="{{ entry.file }}" download>Download {{ 'SKILL.md' if entry.kind == 'skill' else entry.name + '.md' }} ↓</a><a href="{{ entry.source.url }}">View source on GitHub ↗</a></p>
<p class="library-note">This workflow discovers the target repository’s tools and conventions at use time. Read the instructions for its scope and required evidence.</p>

</section>
<section class="library-instructions"><div class="library-section-heading"><h2>The instructions</h2><span>{{ entry.runtime }}</span></div><div class="library-markdown">{{ entry.body | skillMarkdown | safe }}</div></section>
<details class="library-provenance"><summary>Definition metadata & checksum</summary><dl><dt>Source path</dt><dd>{{ entry.source.path }}</dd><dt>SHA-256</dt><dd>{{ entry.sha256 }}</dd></dl></details>
</main>
<script src="/library/library.js" defer></script>
